/-!
# A dual certificate for the modular C6 obstruction

For the regular cyclic action on six variables over `ZMod 3`, this file gives
17 explicit linear functionals on the 132 degree-seven monomial-orbit
coordinates.  They annihilate every one of the 159 products

`e_i * (a lower-degree cyclic orbit sum)`

and pair as the identity matrix with 17 coordinate test vectors.  The generic
dual-certificate lemma therefore proves that the corresponding 17 quotient
classes are linearly independent.

This is intentionally weaker, and much easier to audit, than an exact matrix
rank calculation: it proves the only bound needed for the counterexample,
namely that the quotient needs at least 17 generators.  Every finite identity
is re-evaluated by ordinary kernel reduction over the actual field `ZMod 3`.
The sparse supports for the functionals and product rows were generated by
`Tools/generate_lazard_modular_dual_certificate.py` in exactly the order of
`orbitRepresentatives 7`.  A later sharded polynomial bridge checks every
generated row against its literal elementary-symmetric product, so no claim
depends on trusting the generator.
-/

namespace LeanProofs.PolynomialFormulas.LazardInvariantModularDualCertificate

open scoped BigOperators
open Matrix
open LazardDualQuotientCertificate
open LazardInvariantModularCounterexample

set_option autoImplicit false

abbrev DegreeSevenCoordinates := Fin 132 → F3

